From 18c5abec7220bf7c222d7f4744977782d2361f05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 04:11:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 120/144] feat(pypto-x): add native AVX2 W8A8 widening path

Implement contract 0002 C3 / R6 for the AVX2 backend:

- qmatmul_s8s8_s32 is wired through scalar validation -> CPU vector
  plan -> AVX2 lowering -> artifact metadata -> runtime dispatch.  The
  native kernel widens both int8 operands with vpmovsxbw, pairs two
  products with vpmaddwd and accumulates with vpaddd; AVX2 has no VNNI,
  so there is no vpdpbusd and no u8 x s8 sign compensation.
- Capability declaration travels through CapabilitySet (dtypes int8 /
  int32 / float32 / bf16, matrix_capabilities s8s8_s32_widening) and is
  gated by the existing CPUID/XGETBV AVX2 probe; VNNI/dot-product matrix
  kinds are asserted absent from the declaration.
- Probe-gated target entry points implement the remaining three opcodes
  bit-exactly against the C1 goldens: dequantize_s8, single-rounding
  dequantize_epilogue_bf16, and quantize_per_token_s8 (exact FP64 RNE
  semantics for Q1/Q2/Q4/Q5/Q6).  Reserved -128 codes and binary32
  overflow fail closed like the scalar golden.
- Artifact payload 2 -> 3 and native ABI :3 -> :4; old AVX2 artifacts
  fail closed at load.  BF16 packed semantics and the C1/C2 scheme and
  binding ABIs are unchanged; the packed-test version literals move to
  the new fail-closed constants.
- 62 new focused tests: rank-2/3/4 golden differential, K upper bound,
  fail-closed shape/dtype/-128/capability/ABI tampering, the three
  primitive golden differentials, and objdump evidence that the native
  shared object emits AVX2 widening instructions with zero EVEX
  instructions.
